---
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="Silesian University of Technology"
  category="Education | International Academic Mobility"
  year="2026"
  description="International academic mobility semester at the Silesian University of Technology in Gliwice, Poland."
>

  <p slot="intro" class="hero-intro">
    International academic mobility semester in Gliwice, Poland |
    combining engineering studies, environmental analysis,
    IoT communications and multicultural experience.
  </p>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      01 | Mobility
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Engineering in an international environment.
      </h2>

      <p>
        I completed an academic mobility semester at the
        Silesian University of Technology in Gliwice, Poland,
        as part of my engineering degree at ICAM.
      </p>

      <p>
        This experience allowed me to study in a different academic
        environment while developing greater autonomy,
        adaptability and confidence in an international context.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      02 | Academic Focus
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Broadening my engineering perspective.
      </h2>

      <p>
        The semester included coursework related to
        environmental engineering, life-cycle analysis
        and connected systems.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Environmental Analysis</li>
        <li>Environmental Impact in Full Cycle</li>
        <li>IoT Communications</li>
        <li>International technical collaboration</li>
      </ul>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      03 | Environmental Engineering
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Considering the full life cycle.
      </h2>

      <p>
        The environmental analysis courses introduced broader
        considerations around the impact of engineering systems
        over their full life cycle.
      </p>

      <p>
        This approach reinforced the importance of integrating
        environmental constraints alongside technical,
        industrial and economic considerations.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      04 | Connected Systems
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Exploring communication and IoT.
      </h2>

      <p>
        The IoT communication coursework broadened my understanding
        of connected systems and the role of data exchange
        within modern engineering architectures.
      </p>

      <p>
        This complements my mechanical background by providing
        a better understanding of how physical systems,
        sensors and communication technologies can interact.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      05 | International Experience
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Adapting beyond the classroom.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Living and studying abroad required me to adapt quickly
        to a new language, culture and academic organisation.
      </p>

      <p>
        This experience strengthened my independence,
        problem-solving abilities and capacity to collaborate
        in multicultural environments.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      06 | Outcome
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        A broader engineering outlook.
      </h2>

      <p>
        This mobility experience expanded my perspective
        beyond mechanical engineering alone |
        integrating environmental and digital considerations
        into the way I approach technical systems.
      </p>

      <p>
        It also reinforced my interest in pursuing future
        international academic and research opportunities.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>

</ProjectLayout>